# A destructuring `map [:x :y] in <expr>` binder lives only within its own comprehension body:
# reads of `:x`/`:y` inside the body (line 6) resolve cleanly, but a read of `:x` after the
# comprehension closes (line 7) has no visible declaration in scope (spec/grammar.md:137-138;
# spec/execution-model.md:824-826,1254-1255).
:pairs = [[1 2]]
:doubled = map [:x :y] in :pairs [ :x + :y ]
print :x
